---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <title>StoltGallery</title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bitcount+Prop+Double+Ink:wght@100..900&family=Spectral:ital,wght@0,200;0,300;0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;0,800;1,200;1,300;1,400;1,500;1,600;1,700;1,800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.0/css/all.min.css">
  </head>

  <body class="texture-bg">
    
    <div class="lang-switch">
        <a href="/">FR</a>
        <span>|</span>
        <a href="/en/">EN</a>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Title -->
    <section class="intro">
    
      <h1 class="main-title">Stolt Gallery</h1>

      <h2>History</h2>

      <p class="lead">
        A Dialogue Across Centuries, Techniques, and Sensibilities.
      </p>
      <br>
      <p>
        From an old master of the 17th century to a designer of the 21st, what could they possibly have in common?
      </p>
      <br>
      <p>
        Stolt Gallery brings together works that seem to share a common thread: a certain idea of beauty, independent of eras, movements, and styles.
      </p>

      <p>
        Some works find their beauty in their naivety, while others push us toward introspection. All invite us on a journey, to an encounter with an inner world sometimes unsuspected.
      </p>

      <p>
        Art can disturb us, elevate us, soothe us, or simply silence the noise of the mind. Contemplation, ultimately, teaches us about ourselves.
      </p>
      <br>
      <p>
        Stolt’s ambition is to create a harmonious dialogue between the works, their artists, and you.
      </p>
    </section>


    <hr class="divider">

    <!-- Art Gallery -->
    <section>
      <h2>Gallery</h2>

      <div class="gallery">
        {products.map((product, i) => (
          <figure class="art">
            <img
              src={product.images[0]}
              alt={product.name}
              class="cursor-pointer"
              onclick={`document.getElementById('modal-${i}').showModal()`}
            />
      
            <dialog id={`modal-${i}`} class="p-0 rounded-lg backdrop:bg-black/70">
              
              <div class="max-w-4xl w-full">
      
                <!-- IMAGES -->
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
                  {product.images.map((img) => (
                    <img
                      src={img}
                      class="w-full object-cover"
                    />
                  ))}
                </div>
      
                <!-- TEXT -->
                <div class="p-4">
                  <h2 class="font-semibold mb-2">{product.name}</h2>
                  <p class="text-sm whitespace-pre-line">{product.description}</p>
                </div>
      
                <!-- CLOSE -->
                <form method="dialog">
                  <button class="absolute top-2 right-2 bg-black/60 text-white rounded-full w-8 h-8">
                    ✕
                  </button>
                </form>
      
              </div>
      
            </dialog>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer>
      <p>Follow our latest acquisitions on Instagram</p>

      <div class="socials">
        <a href="https://www.instagram.com/stolt.gallery" target="_blank">
          <i class="fa-brands fa-instagram"></i>
        </a>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-top:20px;font-size:0.8rem;">
        © {new Date().getFullYear()} Stolt Gallery
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>